<title>UK: UK Housing Assn loan book sell-off news expected.</title>
<headline>UK Housing Assn loan book sell-off news expected.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government will make an announcement later on Thursday on its plas to sell off its 1.1 billion stg Housing Association loan portfolio, government sources said.</p>
<p>They said the announcement from the Environment Department, expected at or shortly after 1530 gmt, would come in the form of a written answer to a parliamentary question.</p>
<p>Conservative member of parliament David Lidington has a question on Thursday's parliamentary order paper asking: &quot;What plans there are for the sale of the Housing Corporation's loan portfolios to the private sector to proceed?&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
